#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""gen_cleanup.py - regenerate MORNING_CLEANUP.ps1 from the latest backup receipts.

Re-runnable (e.g. at 07:30 and again after uploads finish):

    python -I E:\\research-dense\\tmp\\morning\\gen_cleanup.py            # regenerate script + manifest
    python -I E:\\research-dense\\tmp\\morning\\gen_cleanup.py --summary  # also refresh the tables in CLEANUP_SUMMARY.md

READ-ONLY with respect to everything except this folder. It never deletes, moves or
edits research files; it never opens rclone.conf; it does not run MORNING_CLEANUP.ps1.
It never reads the contents of sealed / CAL / HOLDOUT / chunk-5 / INC1 paths (it only
lists names/sizes of directories when computing the "pending upload" tables, and skips
those subtrees, exactly like the dataops uploader does).

Inputs (all read-only, all under E:\\rd-wt\\reorg3 unless noted):
  driveops/receipts/*.json (+ receipts/md5/*.md5)      mirrored-directory backups
  dataops/receipts/*.json (+ manifests/members/*.md5)  tar.zst archive backups
  dataops/_out/drive_receipts/*.upload.json            older (pre-reorg) archive receipts
  dataops/_out/queue.json, dataops/data_progress.log   what is queued / measured upload rate
  wtclean/inventory/inventory.json, wtclean/receipts   worktree backups
  ws-clean-int/configs/data_registry.toml              hot-data locations
Outputs (this folder only): MORNING_CLEANUP.ps1, cleanup_manifest.json,
  data_registry_cache.toml (+ CLEANUP_SUMMARY.md tables with --summary).
"""
